   "updated": 1,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "WHAT THIS COMPONENT DOES\nThis is the front door. When you type `nettap <something>`, the click library routes it to one function in this file. Some commands start a long-\nrunning process: `watch` (one daemon on the host that captures many containers), `sidecar` (captures one container from inside that container's\nnetwork) and `sidecars` (a manager that starts and repairs sidecars for you). The others are quick one-shots: `attach` / `detach` only write a request\ninto the database for the running `watch` daemon to pick up, and `status` / `analyze` / `report` / `enrich` read the database, print, and exit. cli.py\ndoes little work itself - it builds the pieces from the other modules, starts the background threads, and makes sure every tcpdump is stopped cleanly\non Ctrl+C or `docker stop`.\n\nIN: command-line arguments, SIGTERM / SIGINT\nOUT: running threads and tcpdump processes, rows in SQLite, printed text or an HTML file\nTALKS TO: every other module - this is where they are wired together",
   "originalText": "WHAT THIS COMPONENT DOES\nThis is the front door. When you type `nettap <something>`, the click library routes it to one function in this file. Some commands start a long-\nrunning process: `watch` (one daemon on the host that captures many containers), `sidecar` (captures one container from inside that container's\nnetwork) and `sidecars` (a manager that starts and repairs sidecars for you). The others are quick one-shots: `attach` / `detach` only write a request\ninto the database for the running `watch` daemon to pick up, and `status` / `analyze` / `report` / `enrich` read the database, print, and exit. cli.py\ndoes little work itself - it builds the pieces from the other modules, starts the background threads, and makes sure every tcpdump is stopped cleanly\non Ctrl+C or `docker stop`.\n\nIN: command-line arguments, SIGTERM / SIGINT\nOUT: running threads and tcpdump processes, rows in SQLite, printed text or an HTML file\nTALKS TO: every other module - this is where they are wired together",
   "fontSize": 16,
   "fontFamily": 2,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "middle",
   "containerId": "hld-rectangle-6",
   "lineHeight": 1.25,
   "autoResize": true
  },
  {
   "id": "hld-rectangle-8",
   "type": "rectangle",
   "x": 1030.4,
   "y": 1762.0,
   "width": 660,
   "height": 403.0,
   "angle": 0,
   "strokeColor": "#1864ab",
   "backgroundColor": "#e7f5ff",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 2,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "groupIds": [],
