   "versionNonce": 1496886435,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "boundElements": [],
   "updated": 1,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "wakes a polling loop the moment Docker starts or stops a container",
   "originalText": "wakes a polling loop the moment Docker starts or stops a container",
   "fontSize": 17,
   "fontFamily": 2,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25,
   "autoResize": true
  },
  {
   "id": "hld-rectangle-70",
   "type": "rectangle",
   "x": -70,
   "y": 2794.625,
   "width": 2070,
   "height": 210.0,
   "angle": 0,
   "strokeColor": "#343a40",
   "backgroundColor": "#f8f9fa",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 2,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "groupIds": [],
   "frameId": null,
   "roundness": {
    "type": 3
   },
   "seed": 1426256014,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 139586394,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "boundElements": [
    {
     "id": "hld-text-71",
     "type": "text"
    }
   ],
   "updated": 1,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false
  },
  {
   "id": "hld-text-71",
   "type": "text",
   "x": -62,
   "y": 2809.625,
   "width": 2054,
   "height": 180.0,
   "angle": 0,
   "strokeColor": "#343a40",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 2,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "groupIds": [],
   "frameId": null,
   "roundness": null,
   "seed": 130286598,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 1570152712,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "boundElements": [],
   "updated": 1,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "WHAT THIS COMPONENT DOES\nA small helper that makes the system react quickly. The controller and the supervisor normally check Docker every 5 seconds. This module opens\nDocker's live event stream on a background thread and, whenever a container starts, dies or is removed, pokes the loop so it runs right away. It\ndecides nothing and passes no data along - it only says 'something changed, look now'. If the stream breaks it reconnects after 5s, and in the\nmeantime the normal 5-second polling keeps working, so nothing is missed.\n\nIN: Docker's events API (through docker.sock)\nOUT: a threading.Event that gets set\nUSED BY: watch (controller.run) and sidecars (the supervisor loop)",
   "originalText": "WHAT THIS COMPONENT DOES\nA small helper that makes the system react quickly. The controller and the supervisor normally check Docker every 5 seconds. This module opens\nDocker's live event stream on a background thread and, whenever a container starts, dies or is removed, pokes the loop so it runs right away. It\ndecides nothing and passes no data along - it only says 'something changed, look now'. If the stream breaks it reconnects after 5s, and in the\nmeantime the normal 5-second polling keeps working, so nothing is missed.\n\nIN: Docker's events API (through docker.sock)\nOUT: a threading.Event that gets set\nUSED BY: watch (controller.run) and sidecars (the supervisor loop)",
   "fontSize": 16,
   "fontFamily": 2,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "middle",
   "containerId": "hld-rectangle-70",
   "lineHeight": 1.25,
   "autoResize": true
  },
  {
   "id": "hld-rectangle-72",
   "type": "rectangle",
   "x": 1330,
   "y": 3054.625,
   "width": 660,
   "height": 178.0,
   "angle": 0,
   "strokeColor": "#1864ab",
   "backgroundColor": "#e7f5ff",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 2,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "groupIds": [],
   "frameId": null,
   "roundness": {
    "type": 3
   },
   "seed": 1506442652,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 664876774,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "boundElements": [
    {
     "id": "hld-text-73",
     "type": "text"
    }
   ],
   "updated": 1,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false
  },
  {
   "id": "hld-text-73",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 1338,
   "y": 3068.625,
   "width": 644,
   "height": 150.0,
   "angle": 0,
   "strokeColor": "#1864ab",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 2,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "groupIds": [],
   "frameId": null,
   "roundness": null,
   "seed": 1389698625,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 1241130074,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "boundElements": [],
   "updated": 1,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "STEP BY STEP (numbers match the badges)\n1. Docker publishes an event for every container change.\n2. A background thread listens only for container start / die / destroy.\n3. On each event it sets a shared flag (a threading.Event).\n4. The loop waiting on that flag wakes early and reconciles now instead of\n    sleeping out its 5s.\n5. If the stream dies (Docker restarted, socket gone) it waits 5s and reconnects;\n    polling covers the gap.",
   "originalText": "STEP BY STEP (numbers match the badges)\n1. Docker publishes an event for every container change.\n2. A background thread listens only for container start / die / destroy.\n3. On each event it sets a shared flag (a threading.Event).\n4. The loop waiting on that flag wakes early and reconciles now instead of\n    sleeping out its 5s.\n5. If the stream dies (Docker restarted, socket gone) it waits 5s and reconnects;\n    polling covers the gap.",
   "fontSize": 15,
   "fontFamily": 2,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "middle",
   "containerId": "hld-rectangle-72",
   "lineHeight": 1.25,
   "autoResize": true
  },
  {
   "id": "hld-rectangle-74",
   "type": "rectangle",
   "x": 1330,
   "y": 3262.625,
   "width": 660,
   "height": 121.75,
   "angle": 0,
   "strokeColor": "#f08c00",
   "backgroundColor": "#ffec99",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 2,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "groupIds": [],
   "frameId": null,
   "roundness": {
