   "seed": 564244067,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 605441631,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "boundElements": [],
   "updated": 1,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "reconciliation loop: makes running captures match the desired state (watch mode)",
   "originalText": "reconciliation loop: makes running captures match the desired state (watch mode)",
   "fontSize": 17,
   "fontFamily": 2,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25,
   "autoResize": true
  },
  {
   "id": "hld-rectangle-107",
   "type": "rectangle",
   "x": -70,
   "y": 3556.375,
   "width": 2453.6,
   "height": 230.0,
   "angle": 0,
   "strokeColor": "#343a40",
   "backgroundColor": "#f8f9fa",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 2,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "groupIds": [],
   "frameId": null,
   "roundness": {
    "type": 3
   },
   "seed": 8790957,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 312837672,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "boundElements": [
    {
     "id": "hld-text-108",
     "type": "text"
    }
   ],
   "updated": 1,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false
  },
  {
   "id": "hld-text-108",
   "type": "text",
   "x": -62,
   "y": 3571.375,
   "width": 2437.6,
   "height": 200.0,
   "angle": 0,
   "strokeColor": "#343a40",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 2,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "groupIds": [],
   "frameId": null,
   "roundness": null,
   "seed": 899680760,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 1148025345,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "boundElements": [],
   "updated": 1,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "WHAT THIS COMPONENT DOES\nThe brain of `watch` mode. It uses the 'reconcile' pattern (the same idea Kubernetes uses): keep a picture of what SHOULD be captured (desired state),\nlook at what IS being captured (actual state), and fix the difference. Desired state = containers matching the --label given at start-up, plus labels\nand names added later with `nettap attach`. Each pass also restarts any tcpdump that crashed and applies the pcap disk limits. A pass runs every 5\nseconds, or at once when events.py reports a container change. A failing pass is logged and the next one tries again, so a hiccup in the Docker API\nnever kills the daemon.\n\nIN: Docker's container list, the desired_refs / desired_labels tables\nOUT: tcpdumps started / stopped (through capture.py), rows in containers and live_sessions\nCALLED BY: `nettap watch` (cli.py), on the main thread",
   "originalText": "WHAT THIS COMPONENT DOES\nThe brain of `watch` mode. It uses the 'reconcile' pattern (the same idea Kubernetes uses): keep a picture of what SHOULD be captured (desired state),\nlook at what IS being captured (actual state), and fix the difference. Desired state = containers matching the --label given at start-up, plus labels\nand names added later with `nettap attach`. Each pass also restarts any tcpdump that crashed and applies the pcap disk limits. A pass runs every 5\nseconds, or at once when events.py reports a container change. A failing pass is logged and the next one tries again, so a hiccup in the Docker API\nnever kills the daemon.\n\nIN: Docker's container list, the desired_refs / desired_labels tables\nOUT: tcpdumps started / stopped (through capture.py), rows in containers and live_sessions\nCALLED BY: `nettap watch` (cli.py), on the main thread",
   "fontSize": 16,
   "fontFamily": 2,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "middle",
   "containerId": "hld-rectangle-107",
   "lineHeight": 1.25,
   "autoResize": true
  },
  {
   "id": "hld-rectangle-109",
   "type": "rectangle",
   "x": 1713.6,
   "y": 3836.375,
   "width": 660,
   "height": 271.75,
   "angle": 0,
   "strokeColor": "#1864ab",
   "backgroundColor": "#e7f5ff",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 2,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "groupIds": [],
   "frameId": null,
   "roundness": {
    "type": 3
   },
   "seed": 792966007,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 1309562236,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "boundElements": [
    {
     "id": "hld-text-110",
     "type": "text"
    }
   ],
   "updated": 1,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false
  },
  {
   "id": "hld-text-110",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 1721.6,
   "y": 3850.375,
   "width": 644,
   "height": 243.75,
   "angle": 0,
   "strokeColor": "#1864ab",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 2,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "groupIds": [],
   "frameId": null,
   "roundness": null,
   "seed": 1216208521,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 684213371,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "boundElements": [],
   "updated": 1,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "STEP BY STEP (numbers match the badges)\n1. Wait for the next tick (5s) or an early wake-up from events.py.\n2. Refresh the heartbeat in live_sessions so `nettap status` knows the daemon is\n    alive.\n3. Ask the CaptureManager to restart any tcpdump that exited on its own.\n4. Work out which containers should be captured: label match (CLI + database) or\n    named by `nettap attach`.\n5. Compare that with the containers being captured right now.\n6. Missing one? Inspect it (discovery.py), save its details, start its tcpdump\n    (capture.py).\n7. Captured but not wanted any more (stopped, detached)? Stop its tcpdump and\n    delete its live_sessions row.\n8. Delete old pcaps if age / size limits are set, then go back to waiting.",
   "originalText": "STEP BY STEP (numbers match the badges)\n1. Wait for the next tick (5s) or an early wake-up from events.py.\n2. Refresh the heartbeat in live_sessions so `nettap status` knows the daemon is\n    alive.\n3. Ask the CaptureManager to restart any tcpdump that exited on its own.\n4. Work out which containers should be captured: label match (CLI + database) or\n    named by `nettap attach`.\n5. Compare that with the containers being captured right now.\n6. Missing one? Inspect it (discovery.py), save its details, start its tcpdump\n    (capture.py).\n7. Captured but not wanted any more (stopped, detached)? Stop its tcpdump and\n    delete its live_sessions row.\n8. Delete old pcaps if age / size limits are set, then go back to waiting.",
   "fontSize": 15,
   "fontFamily": 2,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "middle",
   "containerId": "hld-rectangle-109",
   "lineHeight": 1.25,
   "autoResize": true
  },
  {
   "id": "hld-rectangle-111",
   "type": "rectangle",
   "x": 1713.6,
   "y": 4138.125,
   "width": 660,
   "height": 178.0,
   "angle": 0,
   "strokeColor": "#f08c00",
   "backgroundColor": "#ffec99",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 2,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "groupIds": [],
   "frameId": null,
   "roundness": {
    "type": 3
   },
   "seed": 2046762209,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 269490964,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "boundElements": [
    {
     "id": "hld-text-112",
     "type": "text"
    }
   ],
   "updated": 1,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false
  },
  {
   "id": "hld-text-112",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 1721.6,
   "y": 4152.125,
   "width": 644,
   "height": 150.0,
   "angle": 0,
   "strokeColor": "#f08c00",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 2,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "groupIds": [],
   "frameId": null,
   "roundness": null,
   "seed": 1482823831,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 1845122138,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "boundElements": [],
   "updated": 1,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "WHY POLLING, NOT JUST EVENTS\n\u2022 `nettap attach web` from another terminal only writes a DB row; the daemon\n  picks it up next cycle with no extra plumbing.\n\u2022 A missed 'die' event can't leave a zombie capture running forever.\nFAILURE HANDLING\n\u2022 Heartbeat runs before the main try: a failing Docker API doesn't mean captures\n  are gone.\n\u2022 Any exception in a pass is logged and the loop continues.",
   "originalText": "WHY POLLING, NOT JUST EVENTS\n\u2022 `nettap attach web` from another terminal only writes a DB row; the daemon\n  picks it up next cycle with no extra plumbing.\n\u2022 A missed 'die' event can't leave a zombie capture running forever.\nFAILURE HANDLING\n\u2022 Heartbeat runs before the main try: a failing Docker API doesn't mean captures\n  are gone.\n\u2022 Any exception in a pass is logged and the loop continues.",
   "fontSize": 15,
   "fontFamily": 2,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "middle",
   "containerId": "hld-rectangle-111",
   "lineHeight": 1.25,
   "autoResize": true
  },
  {
   "id": "hld-rectangle-113",
