   "roundness": null,
   "seed": 2101315414,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 1380653906,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "boundElements": [],
   "updated": 1,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "answers: which interface carries this container's traffic, and how do I reach it?",
   "originalText": "answers: which interface carries this container's traffic, and how do I reach it?",
   "fontSize": 17,
   "fontFamily": 2,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25,
   "autoResize": true
  },
  {
   "id": "hld-rectangle-161",
   "type": "rectangle",
   "x": -70,
   "y": 4488.125,
   "width": 2786.8,
   "height": 270.0,
   "angle": 0,
   "strokeColor": "#343a40",
   "backgroundColor": "#f8f9fa",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 2,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "groupIds": [],
   "frameId": null,
   "roundness": {
    "type": 3
   },
   "seed": 1853976394,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 195443666,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "boundElements": [
    {
     "id": "hld-text-162",
     "type": "text"
    }
   ],
   "updated": 1,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false
  },
  {
   "id": "hld-text-162",
   "type": "text",
   "x": -62,
   "y": 4503.125,
   "width": 2770.8,
   "height": 240.0,
   "angle": 0,
   "strokeColor": "#343a40",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 2,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "groupIds": [],
   "frameId": null,
   "roundness": null,
   "seed": 1495071204,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 1815584892,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "boundElements": [],
   "updated": 1,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "WHAT THIS COMPONENT DOES\nBefore tcpdump can record a container, nettap must know WHERE that container's packets flow. Every container has its own network namespace (a private\nnetwork stack) connected to the host by a virtual cable called a veth pair: one end is eth0 inside the container, the other is an interface on the\nhost such as veth3a1f9c2. Capturing on that host end sees everything the container sends and receives - to the host, to other containers and to the\ninternet. This module reads the container from the Docker API, enters its namespace with nsenter to ask the kernel what kind of interface eth0 is, and\npicks the best place to capture: the host-side veth (normal case), the container's own eth0 from inside (macvlan / ipvlan), every interface from\ninside (several networks or a Swarm overlay), or the host's main interface filtered by port (--network host). The answer comes back as a\nContainerNetInfo object that capture.py uses.\n\nIN: a container ID, the Docker API, /var/run/docker/netns, /sys/class/net\nOUT: ContainerNetInfo: where to capture, plus the container's IPs, ports, labels, start time\nUSED BY: controller.py (watch), and sidecar --docker-api to learn other containers' names",
   "originalText": "WHAT THIS COMPONENT DOES\nBefore tcpdump can record a container, nettap must know WHERE that container's packets flow. Every container has its own network namespace (a private\nnetwork stack) connected to the host by a virtual cable called a veth pair: one end is eth0 inside the container, the other is an interface on the\nhost such as veth3a1f9c2. Capturing on that host end sees everything the container sends and receives - to the host, to other containers and to the\ninternet. This module reads the container from the Docker API, enters its namespace with nsenter to ask the kernel what kind of interface eth0 is, and\npicks the best place to capture: the host-side veth (normal case), the container's own eth0 from inside (macvlan / ipvlan), every interface from\ninside (several networks or a Swarm overlay), or the host's main interface filtered by port (--network host). The answer comes back as a\nContainerNetInfo object that capture.py uses.\n\nIN: a container ID, the Docker API, /var/run/docker/netns, /sys/class/net\nOUT: ContainerNetInfo: where to capture, plus the container's IPs, ports, labels, start time\nUSED BY: controller.py (watch), and sidecar --docker-api to learn other containers' names",
   "fontSize": 16,
   "fontFamily": 2,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "middle",
   "containerId": "hld-rectangle-161",
   "lineHeight": 1.25,
   "autoResize": true
  },
  {
   "id": "hld-rectangle-163",
   "type": "rectangle",
   "x": 2046.8000000000002,
   "y": 4808.125,
   "width": 660,
   "height": 309.25,
   "angle": 0,
   "strokeColor": "#1864ab",
   "backgroundColor": "#e7f5ff",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 2,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "groupIds": [],
   "frameId": null,
   "roundness": {
    "type": 3
   },
   "seed": 560740613,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 1113248781,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "boundElements": [
    {
     "id": "hld-text-164",
     "type": "text"
    }
   ],
   "updated": 1,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false
  },
  {
   "id": "hld-text-164",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 2054.8,
   "y": 4822.125,
   "width": 644,
   "height": 281.25,
   "angle": 0,
   "strokeColor": "#1864ab",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 2,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "groupIds": [],
   "frameId": null,
   "roundness": null,
   "seed": 787481804,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 1950470379,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "boundElements": [],
   "updated": 1,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "STEP BY STEP (numbers match the badges)\n1. Read the container from the Docker API: name, IPs, ports, labels, and the\n    SandboxKey (the path to its network-namespace file).\n2. Does it use --network host? Then it has no namespace of its own.\n3. Yes: capture on the host's main interface, and later keep only its ports\n    (hostports.py).\n4. No: enter its namespace and run `ip -j -d link` to learn eth0's type and the\n    index of the other end of its cable.\n5. Decide by the type of link.\n6. Several data interfaces (more than one network, Swarm overlay): capture all of\n    them but lo, inside the namespace.\n7. macvlan / ipvlan have no veth: capture eth0 from inside the namespace.\n8. veth: find the host interface with that index, check it points back at eth0,\n    capture there.\n9. Pack the answer and all metadata into a ContainerNetInfo.",
   "originalText": "STEP BY STEP (numbers match the badges)\n1. Read the container from the Docker API: name, IPs, ports, labels, and the\n    SandboxKey (the path to its network-namespace file).\n2. Does it use --network host? Then it has no namespace of its own.\n3. Yes: capture on the host's main interface, and later keep only its ports\n    (hostports.py).\n4. No: enter its namespace and run `ip -j -d link` to learn eth0's type and the\n    index of the other end of its cable.\n5. Decide by the type of link.\n6. Several data interfaces (more than one network, Swarm overlay): capture all of\n    them but lo, inside the namespace.\n7. macvlan / ipvlan have no veth: capture eth0 from inside the namespace.\n8. veth: find the host interface with that index, check it points back at eth0,\n    capture there.\n9. Pack the answer and all metadata into a ContainerNetInfo.",
   "fontSize": 15,
   "fontFamily": 2,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "middle",
   "containerId": "hld-rectangle-163",
   "lineHeight": 1.25,
   "autoResize": true
  },
