   "autoResize": true
  },
  {
   "id": "hld-text-220",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 153.84000000000003,
   "y": 5493.875,
   "width": 771.1200000000001,
   "height": 21.25,
   "angle": 0,
   "strokeColor": "#495057",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 2,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "groupIds": [],
   "frameId": null,
   "roundness": null,
   "seed": 1731949819,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 1408444750,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "boundElements": [],
   "updated": 1,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "CaptureManager: owns one tcpdump per container (+ one for DNS) and its pcap files",
   "originalText": "CaptureManager: owns one tcpdump per container (+ one for DNS) and its pcap files",
   "fontSize": 17,
   "fontFamily": 2,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25,
   "autoResize": true
  },
  {
   "id": "hld-rectangle-221",
   "type": "rectangle",
   "x": -70,
   "y": 5534.875,
   "width": 2837.2,
   "height": 230.0,
   "angle": 0,
   "strokeColor": "#343a40",
   "backgroundColor": "#f8f9fa",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 2,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "groupIds": [],
   "frameId": null,
   "roundness": {
    "type": 3
   },
   "seed": 313906941,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 1313343736,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "boundElements": [
    {
     "id": "hld-text-222",
     "type": "text"
    }
   ],
   "updated": 1,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false
  },
  {
   "id": "hld-text-222",
   "type": "text",
   "x": -62,
   "y": 5549.875,
   "width": 2821.2,
   "height": 200.0,
   "angle": 0,
   "strokeColor": "#343a40",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 2,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "groupIds": [],
   "frameId": null,
   "roundness": null,
   "seed": 1774917740,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 1279621630,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "boundElements": [],
   "updated": 1,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "WHAT THIS COMPONENT DOES\nRuns and looks after the tcpdump processes. For each container it starts one tcpdump on the interface discovery.py chose, writing raw packets to\ndata/pcap/<name>_<timestamp>.pcap and starting a new file every 60 seconds. It also starts a second, small tcpdump on the container's loopback (lo)\nthat records only lookups to Docker's built-in DNS server 127.0.0.11, because those never cross eth0. tcpdump flushes each packet straight to disk, so\nthe files can be read while they are still being written. The CaptureManager keeps a table of these processes so it can restart ones that crash, stop\nthem on detach, delete old files, and kill leftovers from an earlier crash.\n\nIN: a ContainerNetInfo from discovery.py\nOUT: tcpdump processes; .pcap and .dns.pcap files in data/pcap/ (open them in Wireshark)\nCALLED BY: controller.py (watch) and the sidecar loop in cli.py",
   "originalText": "WHAT THIS COMPONENT DOES\nRuns and looks after the tcpdump processes. For each container it starts one tcpdump on the interface discovery.py chose, writing raw packets to\ndata/pcap/<name>_<timestamp>.pcap and starting a new file every 60 seconds. It also starts a second, small tcpdump on the container's loopback (lo)\nthat records only lookups to Docker's built-in DNS server 127.0.0.11, because those never cross eth0. tcpdump flushes each packet straight to disk, so\nthe files can be read while they are still being written. The CaptureManager keeps a table of these processes so it can restart ones that crash, stop\nthem on detach, delete old files, and kill leftovers from an earlier crash.\n\nIN: a ContainerNetInfo from discovery.py\nOUT: tcpdump processes; .pcap and .dns.pcap files in data/pcap/ (open them in Wireshark)\nCALLED BY: controller.py (watch) and the sidecar loop in cli.py",
   "fontSize": 16,
   "fontFamily": 2,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "middle",
   "containerId": "hld-rectangle-221",
   "lineHeight": 1.25,
   "autoResize": true
  },
  {
   "id": "hld-rectangle-223",
   "type": "rectangle",
   "x": 2097.2,
   "y": 5814.875,
   "width": 660,
   "height": 365.5,
   "angle": 0,
   "strokeColor": "#1864ab",
   "backgroundColor": "#e7f5ff",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 2,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "groupIds": [],
   "frameId": null,
   "roundness": {
    "type": 3
   },
   "seed": 2105190988,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 1018673751,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "boundElements": [
    {
     "id": "hld-text-224",
     "type": "text"
    }
   ],
   "updated": 1,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false
  },
  {
   "id": "hld-text-224",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 2105.2,
   "y": 5828.875,
   "width": 644,
   "height": 337.5,
   "angle": 0,
   "strokeColor": "#1864ab",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 2,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "groupIds": [],
   "frameId": null,
   "roundness": null,
   "seed": 1411472909,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 2013196150,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "boundElements": [],
   "updated": 1,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "STEP BY STEP (numbers match the badges)\n1. The controller or sidecar asks to capture a container.\n2. Give up, with a log line, if there is no interface, or it's a host-network\n    container whose ports can't be attributed to it.\n3. If the capture must run inside the container's namespace (watch mode), put\n    nsenter in front of the command.\n4. Build the tcpdump command: interface, file-name pattern, new file every 60s\n    (-G), flush every packet (-U).\n5. Start it. The kernel kills it if nettap dies (PDEATHSIG), and its error output\n    is copied into nettap's log.\n6. Start the second tcpdump on lo for DNS lookups to 127.0.0.11.\n7. Both write rotating pcap files - the raw evidence everything else is built\n    from.\n8. Every pass: restart any tcpdump that exited.\n9. Delete the oldest pcaps beyond the age / size limits.\n10. At start-up: kill tcpdumps left running by a crashed earlier run (pids from\n    live_sessions).\n11. Stopping: SIGTERM, wait up to 5s, then SIGKILL.",
   "originalText": "STEP BY STEP (numbers match the badges)\n1. The controller or sidecar asks to capture a container.\n2. Give up, with a log line, if there is no interface, or it's a host-network\n    container whose ports can't be attributed to it.\n3. If the capture must run inside the container's namespace (watch mode), put\n    nsenter in front of the command.\n4. Build the tcpdump command: interface, file-name pattern, new file every 60s\n    (-G), flush every packet (-U).\n5. Start it. The kernel kills it if nettap dies (PDEATHSIG), and its error output\n    is copied into nettap's log.\n6. Start the second tcpdump on lo for DNS lookups to 127.0.0.11.\n7. Both write rotating pcap files - the raw evidence everything else is built\n    from.\n8. Every pass: restart any tcpdump that exited.\n9. Delete the oldest pcaps beyond the age / size limits.\n10. At start-up: kill tcpdumps left running by a crashed earlier run (pids from\n    live_sessions).\n11. Stopping: SIGTERM, wait up to 5s, then SIGKILL.",
   "fontSize": 15,
   "fontFamily": 2,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "middle",
   "containerId": "hld-rectangle-223",
   "lineHeight": 1.25,
   "autoResize": true
  },
  {
   "id": "hld-rectangle-225",
   "type": "rectangle",
   "x": 2097.2,
   "y": 6210.375,
   "width": 660,
   "height": 196.75,
   "angle": 0,
   "strokeColor": "#f08c00",
   "backgroundColor": "#ffec99",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 2,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "groupIds": [],
   "frameId": null,
   "roundness": {
    "type": 3
   },
   "seed": 752494410,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 334819384,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "boundElements": [
    {
     "id": "hld-text-226",
     "type": "text"
    }
   ],
   "updated": 1,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false
  },
  {
   "id": "hld-text-226",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 2105.2,
   "y": 6224.375,
   "width": 644,
   "height": 168.75,
   "angle": 0,
   "strokeColor": "#f08c00",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 2,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "groupIds": [],
   "frameId": null,
   "roundness": null,
   "seed": 1178238480,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 1177434288,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "boundElements": [],
   "updated": 1,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "HOUSEKEEPING (BOTTOM ROW)\n\u2022 Called by controller / sidecar loop each pass. A tcpdump that dies quietly\n  would otherwise mean 'the report stopped updating' with no error.\nWHY A SECOND CAPTURE ON LO\n\u2022 Containers on user-defined networks ask 127.0.0.11 for DNS over lo, never eth0.\n  Filtered by host, not port: Docker NATs port 53 to a random port.\nWHY -U\n\u2022 Each packet is flushed to disk, so ingest.py can read a file while tcpdump is\n  still writing it.",
   "originalText": "HOUSEKEEPING (BOTTOM ROW)\n\u2022 Called by controller / sidecar loop each pass. A tcpdump that dies quietly\n  would otherwise mean 'the report stopped updating' with no error.\nWHY A SECOND CAPTURE ON LO\n\u2022 Containers on user-defined networks ask 127.0.0.11 for DNS over lo, never eth0.\n  Filtered by host, not port: Docker NATs port 53 to a random port.\nWHY -U\n\u2022 Each packet is flushed to disk, so ingest.py can read a file while tcpdump is\n  still writing it.",
   "fontSize": 15,
   "fontFamily": 2,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "middle",
   "containerId": "hld-rectangle-225",
   "lineHeight": 1.25,
   "autoResize": true
  },
