   "opacity": 100,
   "groupIds": [],
   "frameId": null,
   "roundness": {
    "type": 3
   },
   "seed": 2021858280,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 531836784,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "boundElements": [
    {
     "id": "hld-text-285",
     "type": "text"
    }
   ],
   "updated": 1,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false
  },
  {
   "id": "hld-text-285",
   "type": "text",
   "x": -62,
   "y": 6594.125,
   "width": 2462.8,
   "height": 200.0,
   "angle": 0,
   "strokeColor": "#343a40",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 2,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "groupIds": [],
   "frameId": null,
   "roundness": null,
   "seed": 1501558974,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 1123584174,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "boundElements": [],
   "updated": 1,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "WHAT THIS COMPONENT DOES\nTurns growing pcap files into database rows within seconds. Waiting for a 60-second file to finish would make reports lag, so every 5 seconds this\nmodule reads only the NEW part of each file. A pcap file is a 24-byte header followed by packets, each with its own 16-byte header that gives its\nlength. ingest walks those headers from where it stopped last time, stops before any packet tcpdump is still writing, copies the new packets (plus the\nfile header) into a small temporary pcap, and has enrich.py / tshark parse it. The rows and the new 'read up to here' position are saved in one\ndatabase transaction, so a crash, or two processes reading the same file, can never count a packet twice.\n\nIN: pcap files, the pcap_progress table\nOUT: rows in flows, updated offsets in pcap_progress\nCALLED BY: the enrich loop in cli.py (every 5s) and the one-off `nettap enrich`",
   "originalText": "WHAT THIS COMPONENT DOES\nTurns growing pcap files into database rows within seconds. Waiting for a 60-second file to finish would make reports lag, so every 5 seconds this\nmodule reads only the NEW part of each file. A pcap file is a 24-byte header followed by packets, each with its own 16-byte header that gives its\nlength. ingest walks those headers from where it stopped last time, stops before any packet tcpdump is still writing, copies the new packets (plus the\nfile header) into a small temporary pcap, and has enrich.py / tshark parse it. The rows and the new 'read up to here' position are saved in one\ndatabase transaction, so a crash, or two processes reading the same file, can never count a packet twice.\n\nIN: pcap files, the pcap_progress table\nOUT: rows in flows, updated offsets in pcap_progress\nCALLED BY: the enrich loop in cli.py (every 5s) and the one-off `nettap enrich`",
   "fontSize": 16,
   "fontFamily": 2,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "middle",
   "containerId": "hld-rectangle-284",
   "lineHeight": 1.25,
   "autoResize": true
  },
  {
   "id": "hld-rectangle-286",
   "type": "rectangle",
   "x": 1738.8000000000002,
   "y": 6859.125,
   "width": 660,
   "height": 253.0,
   "angle": 0,
   "strokeColor": "#1864ab",
   "backgroundColor": "#e7f5ff",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 2,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "groupIds": [],
   "frameId": null,
   "roundness": {
    "type": 3
   },
   "seed": 1882345611,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 1881145519,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "boundElements": [
    {
     "id": "hld-text-287",
     "type": "text"
    }
   ],
   "updated": 1,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false
  },
  {
   "id": "hld-text-287",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 1746.8000000000002,
   "y": 6873.125,
   "width": 644,
   "height": 225.0,
   "angle": 0,
   "strokeColor": "#1864ab",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 2,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "groupIds": [],
   "frameId": null,
   "roundness": null,
   "seed": 2023317399,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 1992455312,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "boundElements": [],
   "updated": 1,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "STEP BY STEP (numbers match the badges)\n1. Every 5s, list every pcap file of every running capture.\n2. Look up how far this file has been read (a byte offset) and whether it's\n    finished.\n3. Walk the packet headers from that offset; stop at a half-written packet or one\n    newer than 2s.\n4. Copy the file header + the new packets into a temporary pcap tshark can read.\n5. Parse it into flow rows (enrich.py).\n6. Host-network container? Drop the packets that weren't on its ports\n    (hostports.py).\n7. Save the rows and the new offset together; if another process already saved\n    this part, do nothing.",
   "originalText": "STEP BY STEP (numbers match the badges)\n1. Every 5s, list every pcap file of every running capture.\n2. Look up how far this file has been read (a byte offset) and whether it's\n    finished.\n3. Walk the packet headers from that offset; stop at a half-written packet or one\n    newer than 2s.\n4. Copy the file header + the new packets into a temporary pcap tshark can read.\n5. Parse it into flow rows (enrich.py).\n6. Host-network container? Drop the packets that weren't on its ports\n    (hostports.py).\n7. Save the rows and the new offset together; if another process already saved\n    this part, do nothing.",
   "fontSize": 15,
   "fontFamily": 2,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "middle",
   "containerId": "hld-rectangle-286",
   "lineHeight": 1.25,
   "autoResize": true
  },
  {
   "id": "hld-rectangle-288",
   "type": "rectangle",
   "x": 1738.8000000000002,
   "y": 7142.125,
   "width": 660,
   "height": 196.75,
   "angle": 0,
   "strokeColor": "#f08c00",
   "backgroundColor": "#ffec99",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 2,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "groupIds": [],
   "frameId": null,
   "roundness": {
    "type": 3
   },
   "seed": 557470198,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 1981664003,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "boundElements": [
