   "updated": 1,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "thin tshark wrapper: one pcap in, one flow-row dict per packet out",
   "originalText": "thin tshark wrapper: one pcap in, one flow-row dict per packet out",
   "fontSize": 17,
   "fontFamily": 2,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25,
   "autoResize": true
  },
  {
   "id": "hld-rectangle-333",
   "type": "rectangle",
   "x": -70,
   "y": 7510.875,
   "width": 2512.4,
   "height": 210.0,
   "angle": 0,
   "strokeColor": "#343a40",
   "backgroundColor": "#f8f9fa",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 2,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "groupIds": [],
   "frameId": null,
   "roundness": {
    "type": 3
   },
   "seed": 85014979,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 1945402620,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "boundElements": [
    {
     "id": "hld-text-334",
     "type": "text"
    }
   ],
   "updated": 1,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false
  },
  {
   "id": "hld-text-334",
   "type": "text",
   "x": -62,
   "y": 7525.875,
   "width": 2496.4,
   "height": 180.0,
   "angle": 0,
   "strokeColor": "#343a40",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 2,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "groupIds": [],
   "frameId": null,
   "roundness": null,
   "seed": 1672884256,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 389878645,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "boundElements": [],
   "updated": 1,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "WHAT THIS COMPONENT DOES\nThe translator from raw packets to readable facts. It runs tshark (Wireshark's command-line tool) over a pcap and asks for 17 fields per packet: time,\nsource and destination IP (v4 or v6), ports, protocol name, size, the DNS question and answers, the TLS server name (SNI - the website name in an\nHTTPS connection) and the HTTP Host header. It cleans each line into a Python dict - one row per packet - ready to insert into the flows table. It is\ndeliberately thin, so it could later be swapped for a richer tool such as Zeek.\n\nIN: a pcap path, plus the container ID and name to tag rows with\nOUT: a list of flow-row dicts\nCALLED BY: ingest.py",
   "originalText": "WHAT THIS COMPONENT DOES\nThe translator from raw packets to readable facts. It runs tshark (Wireshark's command-line tool) over a pcap and asks for 17 fields per packet: time,\nsource and destination IP (v4 or v6), ports, protocol name, size, the DNS question and answers, the TLS server name (SNI - the website name in an\nHTTPS connection) and the HTTP Host header. It cleans each line into a Python dict - one row per packet - ready to insert into the flows table. It is\ndeliberately thin, so it could later be swapped for a richer tool such as Zeek.\n\nIN: a pcap path, plus the container ID and name to tag rows with\nOUT: a list of flow-row dicts\nCALLED BY: ingest.py",
   "fontSize": 16,
   "fontFamily": 2,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "middle",
   "containerId": "hld-rectangle-333",
   "lineHeight": 1.25,
   "autoResize": true
  },
  {
   "id": "hld-rectangle-335",
   "type": "rectangle",
   "x": 1772.4,
   "y": 7770.875,
   "width": 660,
   "height": 234.25,
   "angle": 0,
   "strokeColor": "#1864ab",
   "backgroundColor": "#e7f5ff",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 2,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "groupIds": [],
   "frameId": null,
   "roundness": {
    "type": 3
   },
   "seed": 580778569,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 1623017778,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "boundElements": [
    {
     "id": "hld-text-336",
     "type": "text"
    }
   ],
   "updated": 1,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false
  },
  {
   "id": "hld-text-336",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 1780.4,
   "y": 7784.875,
   "width": 644,
   "height": 206.25,
   "angle": 0,
   "strokeColor": "#1864ab",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 2,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "groupIds": [],
   "frameId": null,
   "roundness": null,
   "seed": 278218446,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 1760458282,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "boundElements": [],
   "updated": 1,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "STEP BY STEP (numbers match the badges)\n1. Receive a pcap (usually ingest's temporary chunk).\n2. Run tshark with the field list; the output is CSV, with repeated values joined\n    by |.\n3. Keep the first value of each field - an ICMP error packet carries a copy of\n    another packet's header that must be ignored.\n4. Merge the IPv4/IPv6 and TCP/UDP columns into single src / dst / port fields,\n    and find the transport layer.\n5. Collect every DNS answer address into a JSON list (used later to put names on\n    IPs).\n6. Return one dict per packet.",
   "originalText": "STEP BY STEP (numbers match the badges)\n1. Receive a pcap (usually ingest's temporary chunk).\n2. Run tshark with the field list; the output is CSV, with repeated values joined\n    by |.\n3. Keep the first value of each field - an ICMP error packet carries a copy of\n    another packet's header that must be ignored.\n4. Merge the IPv4/IPv6 and TCP/UDP columns into single src / dst / port fields,\n    and find the transport layer.\n5. Collect every DNS answer address into a JSON list (used later to put names on\n    IPs).\n6. Return one dict per packet.",
   "fontSize": 15,
   "fontFamily": 2,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "middle",
   "containerId": "hld-rectangle-335",
   "lineHeight": 1.25,
   "autoResize": true
  },
  {
   "id": "hld-rectangle-337",
   "type": "rectangle",
