   "boundElements": [],
   "updated": 1,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "WHAT THIS COMPONENT DOES\nHandles a special case. A container started with --network host shares the host's network, so a capture there sees traffic from the whole machine. To\nkeep only that container's traffic, nettap checks which TCP/UDP ports the container's processes hold, 4 times a second, and stores time ranges such as\n'port 8080 belonged to web from 10:01 to 10:05'. When packets are ingested, keep_owned() keeps only those whose host-side port belonged to the\ncontainer at that moment. Sidecar mode finds the sockets through /proc for the target's processes; watch mode asks the kernel with `ss --cgroup` which\ncontainer created each socket.\n\nIN: /proc/<pid>/fd (sidecar) or `ss --cgroup` output (watch)\nOUT: owned_ports rows; flow rows filtered down to the container's own\nUSED BY: the port-sampler threads in cli.py, and ingest.py",
   "originalText": "WHAT THIS COMPONENT DOES\nHandles a special case. A container started with --network host shares the host's network, so a capture there sees traffic from the whole machine. To\nkeep only that container's traffic, nettap checks which TCP/UDP ports the container's processes hold, 4 times a second, and stores time ranges such as\n'port 8080 belonged to web from 10:01 to 10:05'. When packets are ingested, keep_owned() keeps only those whose host-side port belonged to the\ncontainer at that moment. Sidecar mode finds the sockets through /proc for the target's processes; watch mode asks the kernel with `ss --cgroup` which\ncontainer created each socket.\n\nIN: /proc/<pid>/fd (sidecar) or `ss --cgroup` output (watch)\nOUT: owned_ports rows; flow rows filtered down to the container's own\nUSED BY: the port-sampler threads in cli.py, and ingest.py",
   "fontSize": 16,
   "fontFamily": 2,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "middle",
   "containerId": "hld-rectangle-375",
   "lineHeight": 1.25,
   "autoResize": true
  },
  {
   "id": "hld-rectangle-377",
   "type": "rectangle",
   "x": 1722.0,
   "y": 8608.875,
   "width": 660,
   "height": 215.5,
   "angle": 0,
   "strokeColor": "#1864ab",
   "backgroundColor": "#e7f5ff",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 2,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "groupIds": [],
   "frameId": null,
   "roundness": {
    "type": 3
   },
   "seed": 537834622,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 79348129,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "boundElements": [
    {
     "id": "hld-text-378",
     "type": "text"
    }
   ],
   "updated": 1,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false
  },
  {
   "id": "hld-text-378",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 1730.0,
   "y": 8622.875,
   "width": 644,
   "height": 187.5,
   "angle": 0,
   "strokeColor": "#1864ab",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 2,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "groupIds": [],
   "frameId": null,
   "roundness": null,
   "seed": 32955537,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 39586495,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "boundElements": [],
   "updated": 1,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "STEP BY STEP (numbers match the badges)\n1. A sidecar started with --attribute-by-port, sharing the target's process\n    namespace.\n2. Read the socket list of every target process to see which ports it holds.\n3. watch mode, for every host-network container it captures.\n4. Run ss --cgroup and match each socket to a container by its cgroup path.\n5. Every 0.25s, record the ports into owned_ports as time intervals.\n6. During ingest, keep a packet only if its host-side port was owned at that\n    time.\n7. Everything else (other containers, the host itself) is dropped.",
   "originalText": "STEP BY STEP (numbers match the badges)\n1. A sidecar started with --attribute-by-port, sharing the target's process\n    namespace.\n2. Read the socket list of every target process to see which ports it holds.\n3. watch mode, for every host-network container it captures.\n4. Run ss --cgroup and match each socket to a container by its cgroup path.\n5. Every 0.25s, record the ports into owned_ports as time intervals.\n6. During ingest, keep a packet only if its host-side port was owned at that\n    time.\n7. Everything else (other containers, the host itself) is dropped.",
   "fontSize": 15,
   "fontFamily": 2,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "middle",
   "containerId": "hld-rectangle-377",
   "lineHeight": 1.25,
   "autoResize": true
  },
  {
   "id": "hld-rectangle-379",
   "type": "rectangle",
   "x": 1722.0,
   "y": 8854.375,
   "width": 660,
   "height": 178.0,
   "angle": 0,
   "strokeColor": "#f08c00",
   "backgroundColor": "#ffec99",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 2,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "groupIds": [],
   "frameId": null,
   "roundness": {
    "type": 3
   },
