   "text": "WHAT THIS COMPONENT DOES\nAll persistent state lives in one SQLite file (data/nettap.db). Besides storing packet rows, the database is how separate nettap processes talk to\neach other: `nettap attach` writes a request into desired_*, and the watch daemon reads it; the daemon writes what it's capturing into live_sessions,\nand `nettap status` reads it. This module creates the tables (and adds new columns to older databases), and offers a small function for each read and\nwrite so other modules don't write raw SQL for these tables. The diagram shows each table with who writes it (left) and who reads it (right).\n\nFILE: data/nettap.db (SQLite)\nUSED BY: almost every module - each thread opens its own connection",
   "originalText": "WHAT THIS COMPONENT DOES\nAll persistent state lives in one SQLite file (data/nettap.db). Besides storing packet rows, the database is how separate nettap processes talk to\neach other: `nettap attach` writes a request into desired_*, and the watch daemon reads it; the daemon writes what it's capturing into live_sessions,\nand `nettap status` reads it. This module creates the tables (and adds new columns to older databases), and offers a small function for each read and\nwrite so other modules don't write raw SQL for these tables. The diagram shows each table with who writes it (left) and who reads it (right).\n\nFILE: data/nettap.db (SQLite)\nUSED BY: almost every module - each thread opens its own connection",
   "fontSize": 16,
   "fontFamily": 2,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "middle",
   "containerId": "hld-rectangle-421",
   "lineHeight": 1.25,
   "autoResize": true
  },
  {
   "id": "hld-rectangle-423",
   "type": "rectangle",
   "x": 1013.6,
   "y": 9444.375,
   "width": 660,
   "height": 215.5,
   "angle": 0,
   "strokeColor": "#1864ab",
   "backgroundColor": "#e7f5ff",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 2,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "groupIds": [],
   "frameId": null,
   "roundness": {
    "type": 3
   },
   "seed": 2295477,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 720121671,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "boundElements": [
    {
     "id": "hld-text-424",
     "type": "text"
    }
   ],
   "updated": 1,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false
  },
  {
   "id": "hld-text-424",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 1021.6,
   "y": 9458.375,
   "width": 644,
   "height": 187.5,
   "angle": 0,
   "strokeColor": "#1864ab",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 2,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "groupIds": [],
   "frameId": null,
   "roundness": null,
   "seed": 819536903,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 180153606,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "boundElements": [],
   "updated": 1,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "STEP BY STEP (numbers match the badges)\n1. Requests from attach / detach: container names / IDs and labels to capture.\n2. What a daemon is capturing now: tcpdump pids, file patterns and a heartbeat\n    time (a stale row means the daemon died).\n3. Facts about each container: name, IP per network, published ports, start time\n    - used to put names on IPs.\n4. The main data: one row per packet with IPs, ports, protocol, size, DNS, SNI,\n    HTTP Host.\n5. How far each pcap has been parsed, so parsing resumes without duplicates.\n6. When each port belonged to a host-network container.",
   "originalText": "STEP BY STEP (numbers match the badges)\n1. Requests from attach / detach: container names / IDs and labels to capture.\n2. What a daemon is capturing now: tcpdump pids, file patterns and a heartbeat\n    time (a stale row means the daemon died).\n3. Facts about each container: name, IP per network, published ports, start time\n    - used to put names on IPs.\n4. The main data: one row per packet with IPs, ports, protocol, size, DNS, SNI,\n    HTTP Host.\n5. How far each pcap has been parsed, so parsing resumes without duplicates.\n6. When each port belonged to a host-network container.",
   "fontSize": 15,
   "fontFamily": 2,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "middle",
   "containerId": "hld-rectangle-423",
   "lineHeight": 1.25,
   "autoResize": true
  },
  {
   "id": "hld-rectangle-425",
   "type": "rectangle",
   "x": 1013.6,
   "y": 9689.875,
   "width": 660,
   "height": 215.5,
   "angle": 0,
   "strokeColor": "#f08c00",
   "backgroundColor": "#ffec99",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 2,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "groupIds": [],
   "frameId": null,
   "roundness": {
    "type": 3
   },
   "seed": 1019289434,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 598995198,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "boundElements": [
    {
     "id": "hld-text-426",
     "type": "text"
    }
   ],
   "updated": 1,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false
  },
  {
   "id": "hld-text-426",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 1021.6,
   "y": 9703.875,
   "width": 644,
   "height": 187.5,
   "angle": 0,
   "strokeColor": "#f08c00",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 2,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "groupIds": [],
   "frameId": null,
   "roundness": null,
   "seed": 1079677478,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 1408787664,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "boundElements": [],
   "updated": 1,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "KEY IDEA\n\u2022 SQLite is also the message bus: `nettap attach` in one terminal steers a\n  `nettap watch` daemon in another just by writing rows.\n\u2022 connect() creates missing tables and adds columns added after a table's first\n  release (light migrations).\nRULES\n\u2022 One connection per thread.\n\u2022 store_pcap_chunk() is the only atomic multi-step write (rows + offset).\n\u2022 insert_flows / query boundary kept narrow so swapping to Postgres/ClickHouse\n  stays local to this file.",
   "originalText": "KEY IDEA\n\u2022 SQLite is also the message bus: `nettap attach` in one terminal steers a\n  `nettap watch` daemon in another just by writing rows.\n\u2022 connect() creates missing tables and adds columns added after a table's first\n  release (light migrations).\nRULES\n\u2022 One connection per thread.\n\u2022 store_pcap_chunk() is the only atomic multi-step write (rows + offset).\n\u2022 insert_flows / query boundary kept narrow so swapping to Postgres/ClickHouse\n  stays local to this file.",
   "fontSize": 15,
   "fontFamily": 2,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "middle",
   "containerId": "hld-rectangle-425",
   "lineHeight": 1.25,
   "autoResize": true
  },
