   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25,
   "autoResize": true
  },
  {
   "id": "hld-text-501",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 197.52000000000004,
   "y": 10421.5,
   "width": 685.4400000000002,
   "height": 21.25,
   "angle": 0,
   "strokeColor": "#495057",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 2,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "groupIds": [],
   "frameId": null,
   "roundness": null,
   "seed": 1596046910,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 1487963129,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "boundElements": [],
   "updated": 1,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "nettap sidecars: keeps exactly one sidecar container per labelled target",
   "originalText": "nettap sidecars: keeps exactly one sidecar container per labelled target",
   "fontSize": 17,
   "fontFamily": 2,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25,
   "autoResize": true
  },
  {
   "id": "hld-rectangle-502",
   "type": "rectangle",
   "x": -70,
   "y": 10462.5,
   "width": 2120.4,
   "height": 230.0,
   "angle": 0,
   "strokeColor": "#343a40",
   "backgroundColor": "#f8f9fa",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 2,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "groupIds": [],
   "frameId": null,
   "roundness": {
    "type": 3
   },
   "seed": 653730826,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 1333911086,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "boundElements": [
    {
     "id": "hld-text-503",
     "type": "text"
    }
   ],
   "updated": 1,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false
  },
  {
   "id": "hld-text-503",
   "type": "text",
   "x": -62,
   "y": 10477.5,
   "width": 2104.4,
   "height": 200.0,
   "angle": 0,
   "strokeColor": "#343a40",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 2,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "groupIds": [],
   "frameId": null,
   "roundness": null,
   "seed": 1219258965,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 286562392,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "boundElements": [],
   "updated": 1,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "WHAT THIS COMPONENT DOES\nPowers `nettap sidecars`, which automates sidecar mode. A sidecar must share its target's network namespace, and Docker ties that to one particular\ncontainer instance: if the target stops, the sidecar dies; if the target is recreated, the old sidecar points at nothing. The supervisor checks Docker\nevery 5s (and on events) and keeps exactly one healthy sidecar per labelled container: it creates missing ones, starts or restarts ones that fell out\nof step, replaces ones whose target was recreated, and removes ones whose target is gone. A sidecar that crashed for another reason is left alone, so\nit isn't restarted in a loop.\n\nIN: the Docker API: all containers with their labels and state\nOUT: sidecar containers created / started / restarted / removed\nCALLED BY: `nettap sidecars` (cli.py)",
   "originalText": "WHAT THIS COMPONENT DOES\nPowers `nettap sidecars`, which automates sidecar mode. A sidecar must share its target's network namespace, and Docker ties that to one particular\ncontainer instance: if the target stops, the sidecar dies; if the target is recreated, the old sidecar points at nothing. The supervisor checks Docker\nevery 5s (and on events) and keeps exactly one healthy sidecar per labelled container: it creates missing ones, starts or restarts ones that fell out\nof step, replaces ones whose target was recreated, and removes ones whose target is gone. A sidecar that crashed for another reason is left alone, so\nit isn't restarted in a loop.\n\nIN: the Docker API: all containers with their labels and state\nOUT: sidecar containers created / started / restarted / removed\nCALLED BY: `nettap sidecars` (cli.py)",
   "fontSize": 16,
   "fontFamily": 2,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "middle",
   "containerId": "hld-rectangle-502",
   "lineHeight": 1.25,
   "autoResize": true
  },
  {
   "id": "hld-rectangle-504",
   "type": "rectangle",
   "x": 1380.4,
   "y": 10742.5,
   "width": 660,
   "height": 253.0,
   "angle": 0,
   "strokeColor": "#1864ab",
   "backgroundColor": "#e7f5ff",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 2,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "groupIds": [],
   "frameId": null,
   "roundness": {
    "type": 3
   },
   "seed": 26777431,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 1035990566,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "boundElements": [
    {
     "id": "hld-text-505",
     "type": "text"
    }
   ],
   "updated": 1,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false
  },
  {
   "id": "hld-text-505",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 1388.4,
   "y": 10756.5,
   "width": 644,
   "height": 225.0,
   "angle": 0,
   "strokeColor": "#1864ab",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 2,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "groupIds": [],
   "frameId": null,
   "roundness": null,
   "seed": 130268530,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 1043243375,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "boundElements": [],
   "updated": 1,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "STEP BY STEP (numbers match the badges)\n1. Run a pass on every tick or Docker event.\n2. List the containers and split them into targets (label match) and our sidecars\n    (found by their nettap.sidecar.* labels).\n3. Compare each target with its sidecar.\n4. No sidecar yet: create nettap-sidecar-<name> sharing the target's network.\n5. The sidecar was made for an older container with that name: replace it.\n6. The target restarted after its sidecar started: restart the sidecar so it\n    rejoins.\n7. The sidecar exited because its target stopped (code 3): start it again.\n8. The sidecar crashed for another reason: warn once and leave it alone.\n9. Finally, remove sidecars whose target no longer exists or no longer matches.",
   "originalText": "STEP BY STEP (numbers match the badges)\n1. Run a pass on every tick or Docker event.\n2. List the containers and split them into targets (label match) and our sidecars\n    (found by their nettap.sidecar.* labels).\n3. Compare each target with its sidecar.\n4. No sidecar yet: create nettap-sidecar-<name> sharing the target's network.\n5. The sidecar was made for an older container with that name: replace it.\n6. The target restarted after its sidecar started: restart the sidecar so it\n    rejoins.\n7. The sidecar exited because its target stopped (code 3): start it again.\n8. The sidecar crashed for another reason: warn once and leave it alone.\n9. Finally, remove sidecars whose target no longer exists or no longer matches.",
   "fontSize": 15,
   "fontFamily": 2,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "middle",
   "containerId": "hld-rectangle-504",
   "lineHeight": 1.25,
   "autoResize": true
  },
  {
   "id": "hld-rectangle-506",
   "type": "rectangle",
   "x": 1380.4,
   "y": 11025.5,
   "width": 660,
   "height": 196.75,
   "angle": 0,
   "strokeColor": "#f08c00",
   "backgroundColor": "#ffec99",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 2,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "groupIds": [],
   "frameId": null,
   "roundness": {
    "type": 3
   },
   "seed": 577185114,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 2088447191,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "boundElements": [
    {
     "id": "hld-text-507",
     "type": "text"
    }
   ],
   "updated": 1,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false
  },
  {
   "id": "hld-text-507",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 1388.4,
   "y": 11039.5,
   "width": 644,
   "height": 168.75,
   "angle": 0,
   "strokeColor": "#f08c00",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 2,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "groupIds": [],
   "frameId": null,
   "roundness": null,
   "seed": 1443112403,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 213715570,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "boundElements": [],
   "updated": 1,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "WHY IT EXISTS\n\u2022 A sidecar joins its target's netns once. When the target stops, Docker removes\n  the shared eth0 and the sidecar exits (code 3); Docker restart policies give up\n  too early.\nBOOKKEEPING\n\u2022 Sidecars carry labels nettap.sidecar.target / target-id / selector, so two\n  supervisors with different selectors leave each other alone.\n\u2022 A crashing sidecar isn't restarted in a loop. On shutdown, sidecars are stopped\n  (pcaps flushed) and removed in parallel, unless --keep-sidecars.",
   "originalText": "WHY IT EXISTS\n\u2022 A sidecar joins its target's netns once. When the target stops, Docker removes\n  the shared eth0 and the sidecar exits (code 3); Docker restart policies give up\n  too early.\nBOOKKEEPING\n\u2022 Sidecars carry labels nettap.sidecar.target / target-id / selector, so two\n  supervisors with different selectors leave each other alone.\n\u2022 A crashing sidecar isn't restarted in a loop. On shutdown, sidecars are stopped\n  (pcaps flushed) and removed in parallel, unless --keep-sidecars.",
   "fontSize": 15,
   "fontFamily": 2,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "middle",
   "containerId": "hld-rectangle-506",
   "lineHeight": 1.25,
   "autoResize": true
  },
