   "text": "11. analyze.py",
   "originalText": "11. analyze.py",
   "fontSize": 26,
   "fontFamily": 2,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25,
   "autoResize": true
  },
  {
   "id": "hld-text-554",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 153.84000000000003,
   "y": 11822.75,
   "width": 609.2800000000001,
   "height": 21.25,
   "angle": 0,
   "strokeColor": "#495057",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 2,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "groupIds": [],
   "frameId": null,
   "roundness": null,
   "seed": 1531206449,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 25171971,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "boundElements": [],
   "updated": 1,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "read-side SQL over flows + containers; output is JSON or a table",
   "originalText": "read-side SQL over flows + containers; output is JSON or a table",
   "fontSize": 17,
   "fontFamily": 2,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25,
   "autoResize": true
  },
  {
   "id": "hld-rectangle-555",
   "type": "rectangle",
   "x": -70,
   "y": 11863.75,
   "width": 2128.8,
   "height": 230.0,
   "angle": 0,
   "strokeColor": "#343a40",
   "backgroundColor": "#f8f9fa",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 2,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "groupIds": [],
   "frameId": null,
   "roundness": {
    "type": 3
   },
   "seed": 1936099449,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 1588939959,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "boundElements": [
    {
     "id": "hld-text-556",
     "type": "text"
    }
   ],
   "updated": 1,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false
  },
  {
   "id": "hld-text-556",
   "type": "text",
   "x": -62,
   "y": 11878.75,
   "width": 2112.8,
   "height": 200.0,
   "angle": 0,
   "strokeColor": "#343a40",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 2,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "groupIds": [],
   "frameId": null,
   "roundness": null,
   "seed": 622411543,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 543769092,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "boundElements": [],
   "updated": 1,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "WHAT THIS COMPONENT DOES\nAnswers questions about the captured traffic with SQL over the flows and containers tables. Who talked the most? Which containers talk to each other?\nWhich internet addresses and hostnames were contacted? What DNS lookups happened? Which protocols were used? Helper functions do the tricky parts:\ndeciding which container owned an IP when a packet was sent (IPs get reused when containers are recreated), whether an IP is on the internet or local,\nand the best name for an IP (from TLS SNI, HTTP Host or DNS answers). Results are lists of dicts, printed as JSON or a table, and report.py reuses\nthem.\n\nIN: the flows and containers tables\nOUT: lists of dicts (JSON, or a table with --format table)\nUSED BY: `nettap analyze ...` and report.py",
   "originalText": "WHAT THIS COMPONENT DOES\nAnswers questions about the captured traffic with SQL over the flows and containers tables. Who talked the most? Which containers talk to each other?\nWhich internet addresses and hostnames were contacted? What DNS lookups happened? Which protocols were used? Helper functions do the tricky parts:\ndeciding which container owned an IP when a packet was sent (IPs get reused when containers are recreated), whether an IP is on the internet or local,\nand the best name for an IP (from TLS SNI, HTTP Host or DNS answers). Results are lists of dicts, printed as JSON or a table, and report.py reuses\nthem.\n\nIN: the flows and containers tables\nOUT: lists of dicts (JSON, or a table with --format table)\nUSED BY: `nettap analyze ...` and report.py",
   "fontSize": 16,
   "fontFamily": 2,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "middle",
   "containerId": "hld-rectangle-555",
   "lineHeight": 1.25,
   "autoResize": true
  },
  {
   "id": "hld-rectangle-557",
   "type": "rectangle",
   "x": 1388.8000000000002,
   "y": 12143.75,
   "width": 660,
   "height": 234.25,
   "angle": 0,
   "strokeColor": "#1864ab",
   "backgroundColor": "#e7f5ff",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 2,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "groupIds": [],
   "frameId": null,
   "roundness": {
    "type": 3
   },
   "seed": 799340671,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 139537805,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "boundElements": [
    {
     "id": "hld-text-558",
     "type": "text"
    }
   ],
   "updated": 1,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false
  },
  {
   "id": "hld-text-558",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 1396.8000000000002,
   "y": 12157.75,
   "width": 644,
   "height": 206.25,
   "angle": 0,
   "strokeColor": "#1864ab",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 2,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "groupIds": [],
   "frameId": null,
   "roundness": null,
   "seed": 843744994,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 837864501,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "boundElements": [],
   "updated": 1,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "STEP BY STEP (numbers match the badges)\n1. Start from the stored flow rows and container facts.\n2. Map an IP to the container that held it when the packet was sent.\n3. Classify an IP as internet or local, with hints such as 'Docker Desktop DNS'.\n4. Find a hostname for each IP from SNI, HTTP Host or DNS answers.\n5. Biggest source \u2192 destination pairs by bytes.\n6. Container-to-container traffic, direct or through a published port.\n7. Traffic leaving Docker: destinations that belong to no container, with names.\n8. The DNS names that were looked up.\n9. The share of each protocol.\n10. Print as JSON (for scripts) or an aligned table (for people).",
   "originalText": "STEP BY STEP (numbers match the badges)\n1. Start from the stored flow rows and container facts.\n2. Map an IP to the container that held it when the packet was sent.\n3. Classify an IP as internet or local, with hints such as 'Docker Desktop DNS'.\n4. Find a hostname for each IP from SNI, HTTP Host or DNS answers.\n5. Biggest source \u2192 destination pairs by bytes.\n6. Container-to-container traffic, direct or through a published port.\n7. Traffic leaving Docker: destinations that belong to no container, with names.\n8. The DNS names that were looked up.\n9. The share of each protocol.\n10. Print as JSON (for scripts) or an aligned table (for people).",
   "fontSize": 15,
   "fontFamily": 2,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "middle",
   "containerId": "hld-rectangle-557",
   "lineHeight": 1.25,
   "autoResize": true
  },
  {
   "id": "hld-rectangle-559",
   "type": "rectangle",
   "x": 1388.8000000000002,
   "y": 12408.0,
   "width": 660,
   "height": 196.75,
   "angle": 0,
   "strokeColor": "#f08c00",
   "backgroundColor": "#ffec99",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 2,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "groupIds": [],
   "frameId": null,
   "roundness": {
    "type": 3
   },
   "seed": 2144890576,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 1868250484,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "boundElements": [
    {
     "id": "hld-text-560",
     "type": "text"
    }
   ],
   "updated": 1,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false
  },
  {
   "id": "hld-text-560",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 1396.8000000000002,
   "y": 12422.0,
   "width": 644,
   "height": 168.75,
   "angle": 0,
   "strokeColor": "#f08c00",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 2,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "groupIds": [],
   "frameId": null,
   "roundness": null,
   "seed": 1265247240,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 164069245,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "boundElements": [],
   "updated": 1,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "KEY IDEA\n\u2022 Each flow belongs to the capture it came from (container_name). The peer is\n  found by matching dst_ip to a container's address at the packet's time - IPs\n  get reused when containers are recreated.\n\u2022 Traffic to the host on a port another container publishes counts as container-\n  to-container ('published port').\nUSED BY\n\u2022 `nettap analyze ...` directly, and report.py for the plain-language summary.\n  top_talkers, dns_queries and protocol_breakdown read flows directly.",
   "originalText": "KEY IDEA\n\u2022 Each flow belongs to the capture it came from (container_name). The peer is\n  found by matching dst_ip to a container's address at the packet's time - IPs\n  get reused when containers are recreated.\n\u2022 Traffic to the host on a port another container publishes counts as container-\n  to-container ('published port').\nUSED BY\n\u2022 `nettap analyze ...` directly, and report.py for the plain-language summary.\n  top_talkers, dns_queries and protocol_breakdown read flows directly.",
   "fontSize": 15,
   "fontFamily": 2,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "middle",
   "containerId": "hld-rectangle-559",
   "lineHeight": 1.25,
   "autoResize": true
  },
